  fallback behavior.

  I don't know your real hostnames or non-prod endpoint URLs, so I'll put clearly-marked placeholders in the table for
  anything you don't give me — the existing [38;5;153mhttps://api.example.com/login[39m is itself a placeholder, so production may
  need one too. Unknown hostnames will fall back to production rather than throwing, since a page that silently can't
  log in is worse than one that points at prod.

[38;5;246m⏺ [39mUser answered Claude's questions:
