[38;5;231m⏺[39m One more before the design — this repo has no test runner, no linter, and a [38;5;153mpackage.json[39m with no scripts or
  dependencies. Cheapest moment to add tooling is now, but there's a real tension worth naming:

  The environment resolver (hostname + [38;5;153m?env=[39m override → endpoint) is pure logic and the only part of this worth testing.
  To unit-test it under Node, [38;5;153msettings.js[39m needs a small [38;5;153mif (typeof module !== "undefined") module.exports = ...[39m guard
  at the bottom — the dual-format trick we just declined for [3mconsumers[0m, used here only so tests can import it. It's a
  common pattern and costs three lines, but it's a wart on a file we agreed would be browser-only. The alternative is
  verifying by loading [38;5;153mindex.html[39m and checking [38;5;153mwindow.SETTINGS[39m in the console, which tests nothing automatically.

  Node's built-in [38;5;153mnode:test[39m needs no dependencies at all. A linter would mean adding ESLint plus config to a
  zero-dependency repo.

